From 0d0dc5688bb6e070f4b8a88bd61e89f96e3e7fc2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mira <mira@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 28 May 2026 23:30:46 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] [feature](be) Refactor native stack collector to
 ob-kill60 inline coordinator

Replaces the freeform per-slot atomic + poll-loop collector with an
OceanBase-style two-phase coordinator that runs inline from the HTTP
action thread. Per-thread series under g_sig_handler_ctx_.lock():

  1. atomic_set_req_id + record target tid (anti-spoof token)
  2. pipe2(O_CLOEXEC) for fd_ (worker->coord) and fd2_ (coord->worker)
  3. rt_tgsigqueueinfo(sival_ptr=req_id) primary, tgkill fallback
  4. poll fd_ for prepare-ack (worker filled ctx.frames_)
  5. copy frames out of ctx into the per-request ThreadResult
  6. write process-done on fd2_, poll fd_ for exit-ack
  7. close pipes, atomic_set_req_id(0)

DSO offsets are computed in the coordinator after the lock is released
(Phase 2 plan line 391: yes, this design pauses workers while the
coordinator computes DSO offsets). ObProcMaps::load_maps() refreshes
/proc/self/maps once per request so dlopen()'d libs show up.

Reference: <ob>/deps/oblib/src/lib/signal/ob_signal_worker.cpp:99-141
Reference: <ob>/deps/oblib/src/lib/signal/ob_signal_worker.cpp:280-347
Reference: <ob>/deps/oblib/src/lib/signal/ob_signal_handlers.cpp:103-120
